Bluetooth: btusb: Add VID:PID 13d3:3530 for Realtek RTL8821CE

The Bluetooth half of the RTL8821CE combo card (AzureWave AW-CB375NF and
similar, Wi-Fi at 10ec:c821 on rtw88_8821ce) enumerates on some laptops
as 13d3:3530. btusb only lists 3529 and 3533 for this chip, so 3530 falls
through to the generic class match: no BTUSB_REALTEK, so btrtl never
runs, rtl_bt/rtl8821c_fw.bin is never loaded, and the controller runs on
its mask ROM. Symptoms: no "hci0: RTL:" lines in dmesg, A2DP links that
drop under Wi-Fi traffic (the ROM has no working coexistence), and
"Unexpected start frame" from L2CAP when ACL fragments go missing.

Give 3530 the same entry as 3529.

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -504,6 +504,8 @@
 	/* Realtek 8821CE Bluetooth devices */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x13d3, 0x3529), .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK |
 						     BTUSB_WIDEBAND_SPEECH },
+	{ USB_DEVICE(0x13d3, 0x3530), .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK |
+						     BTUSB_WIDEBAND_SPEECH },
 
 	/* Realtek 8822CE Bluetooth devices */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x0bda, 0xb00c), .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK |
